  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Urban rhythm born in the early 2000s in the Nkoldongo quarter of Yaoundé at ceremonies, above all funeral vigils, first sung without instruments and close to bikutsi in rhythm. It spread through the city's popular quarters and reached the studio in 2016, when Petit Malo's 'Dans mon Kwatta' became the first studio mbolé recording; djembe is its principal instrument, with maracas and keyboard.",
